@@ -5,6 +5,18 @@
 
 ## 2026-07-20
 
+### 2359 — Runtime model rework closes nested-version and fail-safe projection gaps (TASK-260715-lovbdz)
+- REGRESSION: A schema-v1 `RuntimeStartRequest` previously accepted a nested `TunnelConfigurationReference` at schema 0 or 2 because only the outer header was checked. The nested decoder now returns the same stable `unsupportedSchemaVersion` error for both old and future versions.
+- SAFETY: A future lifecycle `routeState` previously decoded as `unknown` while preserving true TCP, safe-DNS, route-installed, and health facts. Route state now participates in the shared fail-safe projection for both decoded and directly constructed lifecycle snapshots, forcing every capability false when it is unknown.
+- COMPATIBILITY: Diagnostics generation and sequence remain required, while absent counters, gauges, histograms, and errors decode to their documented empty defaults. Explicit `null` or a wrong type remains corrupt rather than being treated as absence.
+- VERIFICATION: Focused runtime codec tests and `make validate-core` pass; the full gate reports 183 tests in 21 suites plus boundary/native-package checks and a post-test build. Repository-wide Swift format lint, `git diff --check`, and `task-board validate` are clean.
+
+### 2344 — Runtime wire models make shared configuration secret-free by construction (TASK-260715-lovbdz)
+- DECISION: M1 app messages use sorted-key protocol/schema v1 JSON with per-family 4/16/64 KiB limits and a strict bounded preflight that rejects invalid UTF-8, duplicate keys (including escape-equivalent keys), excessive nesting, corrupt numbers, trailing bytes, unsupported versions/kinds/values, and missing required fields before model use. The legacy `version` request/response remains the exact two-field v1 exception.
+- SECURITY: The prior `TunnelConfiguration.parameters: [String:String]` escape hatch made private-key/passphrase exclusion structurally impossible. It was removed; provider/start configuration now contains only a schema-v1 UUID-backed profile reference, while configuration snapshots use distinct UUID-backed profile revision, credential, and trust references. Harness experiment parameters remain in harness-only recorded output and no longer cross into the runtime configuration.
+- CAPABILITY: TCP, safe DNS, UDP, route mode, route-installed state, and health are independent required facts with no full-mode bit. Unknown output lifecycle/route values project to `unknown` with every capability false; generation/sequence ordering rejects lower generations and non-increasing snapshots.
+- VERIFICATION: `make validate-core` passes boundary/native-package checks, 182 Swift tests in 21 suites, and a post-test build; repository-wide Swift format lint is clean. Tests cover every model round-trip, golden bytes, additive fields, old/future versions, hostile/corrupt/oversize input, secret-shape regression, redacted finite errors, legacy compatibility, and both platform roots.
+
 ### 2317 — M1 runtime contract separates structural work from production M0 binding (TASK-260715-30zng6)
 - DECISION: The packet-tunnel extension owns one actor-serialized runtime generation, with immutable app-message snapshots and no live forwarding dependency on the containing app. Startup is configuration -> verified/authenticated SSH -> TCP/DNS readiness -> pure packet preflight -> settings apply -> existing PacketBridge.start/read activation -> TCP + safe-DNS publication; every failure rolls back through one idempotent, non-cancellable stopping path.
 - OWNERSHIP: M1PacketPlaneSession is the sole owner of the HEV private SOCKS boundary and dispatches authenticated CONNECT to TCP plus only approved virtual-DNS UDP/TCP to DNS; other UDP is rejected until M2. The coordinator proceeds against fakes independently of production factories, and both branches converge at TASK-260715-30ugfm.
